{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/87091-splinters-ideas-for-a-berlin-game","id":87091,"title":"Splinters ideas for a Berlin game?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-08T17:07:54-08:00","id":87091,"title":"Splinters ideas for a Berlin game?","content":"I'm beginning the preparations for a Demon game but, while I find the Timeline Splinters really cool (I blame Doctor Who), neither I nor my players are familiar enough with Seattle to play a game set there. Instead of that, we're going to use Berlin and, as the title says, I'm looking for Splinters ideas for that city.<br /> <br /> I've been thinking about a Splinter that's basically a loop of the Berlin Blocade where the tension between the Western Allies and Soviet Union eventually culminates in the city getting destroyed and the week before Kennedy's &quot;Ich bin ein Berliner&quot; speech where JFK gets assassinated instead, but I could use some more.<br /> <br /> Do you have any suggestions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 03-08-2014, 08:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T17:54:13-08:00","id":87110,"title":"","content":"Theres that whole tearing down of the Berlin wall.. you can have a splinter where it never split.. or a splinter where the two halves were never reunited.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2451-windrave","name":"Windrave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2451_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T17:05:36-07:00","id":87809,"title":"","content":"Assuming your players are comfortable with it, it seems to go without saying that you could have a <i>Fatherland</i>-like splinter where the Nazis are still in power years after the war. A lot could be done thematically with the idea of people not really acknowledging that part of their history and literally having a hidden world where it's all still horribly real.<br /> <br /> If not that, i'd have one in 1946 or so where the city is still in ruins, crowded with refugees and Allied soldiers with plenty of places for a person to disappear or change their identity, the God-Machine has a perfect cover for rebuilding the city in line with its own goals, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T09:51:59-07:00","id":88246,"title":"","content":"The first thing you're going to need to decide is when exactly did the God-Machine decide to form splinters. Unlike Seattle, Berlin has a good 600 years more time to play with so, depending on your answer to the question, you may even need to decide what a &quot;Historical&quot; God-Machine looked like.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think exploring the history of the God-Machine set in a backdrop of the Reformation and the Thirty Years' War sounds fun.<br /> <br /> I could also see Berlin after Napoleon conquered it making it nifty splinter as could it's reaction to the proclamation of the German Empire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2037-iceix","name":"IceIX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T10:35:08-07:00","id":88278,"title":"","content":"This also trends on sensitive territory, but there's interwar periods that could be interesting - repeating chunks of time in the rise of the Nazi party, or just hyperinflation.<br /> <br /> A whole different kind of sensitive could be a splinter centered around the 1972 Summer Olympics in Munich.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I'm always a sucker for the thorny topics, but the whole cold war is ripe with demon vibes and intrigue, so any splinter in those decades is interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}